{
  "esm": "1.3.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mom6_cgrid_div_y",
    "description": "The meridional C-grid flux-form divergence rewrite target D(vh, wrt: y) on the mom6_cgrid, the y mirror of mom6_cgrid_div_x: lowers the spatial derivative of the north-face layer volume flux field vh [i,j,k] to the cell divergence div_y(i,j,k) = (vh(i,j,k) - vh(i,j-1,k)) * IareaT(i,j) (the MOM6 continuity convergence (vh(i,j) - vh(i,j-1))*IareaT of continuity_merid_convergence, MOM_continuity_PPM.F90:1564-1573, with vh(i,j) the north-face flux of each cell and vh(i,j-1) the north-face flux of the south neighbor, i.e. the south face of cell (i,j)). SOLID-WALL BOUNDARIES: the south edge of cell j = 1 is a wall whose face flux is identically zero, so the j = 1 region is the EXPLICIT wall divergence div_y(i,1,k) = vh(i,1,k) * IareaT(i,1) — NOT the clamped difference (vh(1) - vh(1))*IareaT = 0 (the bug it replaces, the y mirror of the div_x fix). The north wall is carried by the flux rule, which emits the zero face flux at the north domain edge (j = N_J), so the interior region formula extends to j = N_J unchanged: div_y(i,N_J,k) = (0 - vh(i,N_J-1,k))*IareaT(i,N_J). The rule matches any D(vh, y) whose operand is a declared [i,j,k] field; IareaT is a free name resolved in the consuming model. Pure telescoping difference of the face fluxes; the PPM reconstruction lives in the sibling mom6_cgrid_flux_y rule.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:mom6_cgrid",
      "grid:mom6_cgrid",
      "op:div",
      "order:1",
      "bc:wall",
      "axes:i,j,k",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Adcroft, A., et al. (2019). The GFDL global ocean and sea ice model OM4.0. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 11(10), 3167-3211.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2019MS001726"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "mom6_cgrid_div_y": {
      "params": ["vh"],
      "priority": 10,
      "match": {
        "op": "D",
        "args": ["vh"],
        "wrt": "y"
      },
      "where": {
        "vh": {
          "shape": ["i", "j", "k"]
        }
      },
      "body": {
        "op": "makearray",
        "args": [],
        "regions": [
          [
            [1, "N_I"],
            [2, "N_J"],
            [1, "N_K"]
          ],
          [
            [1, "N_I"],
            [1, 1],
            [1, "N_K"]
          ]
        ],
        "values": [
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j", "k"],
            "args": ["vh", "IareaT"],
            "ranges": {
              "i": [1, "N_I"],
              "j": [2, "N_J"],
              "k": [1, "N_K"]
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": ["IareaT", "i", "j"]
                },
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": ["vh", "i", "j", "k"]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": ["vh", "i", { "op": "-", "args": ["j", 1] }, "k"]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j", "k"],
            "args": ["vh", "IareaT"],
            "ranges": {
              "i": [1, "N_I"],
              "j": [1, 1],
              "k": [1, "N_K"]
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": ["IareaT", "i", "j"]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": ["vh", "i", "j", "k"]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
